# Keeps `railway up` uploads small. The storefront build needs apps/ plus the
# workspace manifests at the root — nothing else here is read at build time.
#
# Written after a `railway up` upload timed out and left a deployment stuck in
# INITIALIZING with no build attached: the payload was 60MB, of which 55MB was
# product source assets and an image backup the build never opens.
#
# Every directory pattern is ROOT-ANCHORED with a leading slash. Without it,
# gitignore semantics match a directory of that name at ANY depth: a bare
# `products/` also excluded apps/storefront/src/modules/products and the
# products route group, and the build failed on a missing @modules/products
# import. Never write these unanchored.
#
# Do NOT exclude apps/backend: npm workspaces ("apps/**") resolves every
# workspace manifest at install time, so dropping it breaks the install even
# though only the storefront is built.

# Product source assets and generated PDFs (~23MB)
/products/

# Book chapters and the generated book PDF (~1.6MB)
/book/

# One-off backup of product images (~32MB)
/product-images-backup/

# Backups, research notes, and loose assets
/backup_products_*.json
/research/
/brain.jpg

# Docs and agent config — not read by any build step
/.claude/
/CLAUDE.md
/README.md
/LICENSE

# Any stray PDF anywhere; no build step reads one
*.pdf
